  "worked_solution": "We find the constants $A$ and $B$ using the initial conditions. \n\n- Substituting $y(0)=-1$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\nA=-1.\n$$\n\n- To apply the condition ${y}^{′}(0)=8,$ we first differentiate $y$ to get\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=-7A{e}^{-7x}+B{e}^{-7x}-7Bx{e}^{-7x}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${y}^{′}(0)=8$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n-7A+B=8.\n$$\n\nUsing the fact that $A=-1$ gives $B=1.$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny=-{e}^{-7x}+x{e}^{-7x}.\n$$",
